<BaseLayout title="Exhaust & Heat Shielding" description="Header clearance around the fuse box and DEI heat shielding for the tunnel and exhaust on LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Exhaust &amp; Heat Shielding</h1>
  <p>
    Header choice is tied to engine mounts and steering/rack clearance. Sikky headers are the most commonly referenced; ISR headers sit lower and are generally not recommended on lowered cars.
  </p>

  <h2>Headers</h2>
  <p>Header options (Sikky, ISR, CX Racing, custom) are compared on the <a href="/guides/swap-kits#headers">Swap Kits → Headers</a> tab, since they're tied to your motor mounts.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Real-world warning:</strong> on one LS1 Gen Coupe, headers sitting too close caused the main fuse box to catch fire. Check clearance to the fuse box, harness, brake lines, and steering shaft, and shield anything within a few inches.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="heat">Heat Shielding</h2>
  <p>
    LS engines put out a ton of heat. I highly recommend spending the money on a good amount of DEI heat shielding in the tunnel and on the exhaust.
    With no shielding at all my legs were literally frying near the gas pedal. Wrapping only the exhaust helps, but stick-on tunnel shielding together with wrap is best.
  </p>
